course: dictionary
lesson: 14218
title: Musculature: the muscles of the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Musculature is a long, formal word for muscles. Scientists, doctors and PE teachers use it, but in everyday talk people say "muscles." Your body has hundreds of muscles, and musculature means all of them in a body or in one part of it, along with how they are arranged.
explain: «The musculature of her leg was strong from years of running.» Read the clues: leg, strong, running. The sentence is about the muscles in her leg, so musculature must mean those muscles. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "The muscles of her leg were strong from years of running." It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Artists also study musculature. A painter drawing a horse needs to know how its muscles are arranged under the skin, so the picture looks real. When you meet a long word like this, look for a simpler word that fits in the same place, and you will usually find the meaning.
fact: Musculature means all the muscles of a body or of one part of the body, and how they are arranged.
fact: «The musculature of the leg» means the muscles in the leg.
fact: Musculature is a formal, science word; in everyday talk people say "muscles."
fact: Musculature is usually uncountable, so you say "good musculature," not "three musculatures."
fact: Artists study the musculature of animals and people so their drawings look real.
exercise: «The musculature of her leg was strong from years of running.» What does musculature mean? | Shoes worn for running | Bones of the leg | *All the muscles of the leg and how they are arranged | Blood vessels in the skin
exercise: Which everyday word means about the same as musculature? | *muscles | shoes | skin | bones
exercise: Why would an artist study the musculature of a horse before drawing it? | Because horses have no muscles | *So the muscles look right under the skin | To find out what it eats | To count its teeth
test: The coach said, «Stretch the musculature of your arms before you swim.» What does musculature mean here? | Swimming costumes | *The muscles of the arms and how they are arranged | The sound of a whistle | Sleepy feelings
test: Which sentence uses musculature correctly? | I ate a musculature for lunch. | The musculature of the bus was painted red. | The musculature was a sunny afternoon at the park. | *The musculature of the dog's back legs is very strong.
exam: In «the musculature of the back», what does musculature mean? | The clothes worn on the back | The spine | *The muscles of the back and how they are arranged | The skin covering the back
